+<!--
+Write the public commit message the way an upstream maintainer should
+read it. Do not mention the company, internal issue trackers, or private
+hostnames above the cutoff.
+
+The pull request title is the commit subject and the queue entry title.
+The text above the cutoff is the public body. HTML comments are stripped
+when Uplink stores the message.
+-->
+
+<!-- Public body goes here. -->
+
+----- Uplink: internal below this line -----
+
+<!--
+Internal notes below stay on company main and are stripped before export
+to upstream. Do not delete the cutoff line.
+
+Examples:
+Ticket: PROJ-1234
+Uplink-Depends-On: upl_…
+Uplink-Export-Author: Jane Public <jane@users.noreply.github.com>
+
+Uplink-Export-Author adds a Co-Authored-By trailer to the public commit.
+The commit author is the contribution account.
+-->
