+# and including the patch, which becomes the protected base
+# uplink/amend/<id>. A -work branch one empty commit ahead is pushed and a
+# draft PR is opened. Commit the change on -work and edit the PR title and
+# description (they become the patch title and message). Merging runs
+# git uplink amend --complete, which re-assesses the patch and rebuilds
+# company main. If preflight.sh fails on the rebuilt tree, the first patch
+# it fails on (found with git bisect) gets a conflict PR, as in sync. For a
+# submitted patch Uplink submit is dispatched: the patch
+# is amended and needs a delta approval when the amend changes the lines it
+# adds or removes, or the public title or message, and stays submitted when
+# it does not. Closing without merging deletes both branches and leaves the
+# queue unchanged. Closed-PR jobs load YAML from the default branch so *-work
